

Curvature‑Flux Helix Engine — API Specification

Author: C. Matthew Blackwell — Independent Designer

1. Overview

The Curvature‑Flux Helix Engine API provides a unified interface for:

curvature/torsion geometry injection

MRI solver execution

exotic‑matter stability transformation

cryptographic provenance generation

simulation snapshot retrieval

topology visualization hooks

It is designed for GPU clusters, distributed simulation environments, and secure scientific workflows.

2. Base URL

/helix-engine/v1/

3. Authentication

All endpoints require:

X-Shear-Key: <cryptographic-shear-key>
X-Simulation-ID: <uuid>

The shear key is derived from geometry parameters and ensures provenance integrity.

4. Endpoints

4.1 Geometry Initialization

POST /geometry/init

Initializes helix geometry.

Body:

{
  "curvature": "kappa(s)",
  "torsion": "tau(s)",
  "flux_density": "Phi(s)",
  "domain": {
    "r_min": 0.1,
    "r_max": 50.0,
    "z_min": -5.0,
    "z_max": 5.0
  }
}

Response:

{
  "status": "initialized",
  "geometry_id": "<uuid>"
}

4.2 MRI Solver Execution

POST /mri/run

Runs MRI solver with curvature‑flux coupling.

Body:

{
  "geometry_id": "<uuid>",
  "angular_velocity": "Omega(r)",
  "seed_field": "B0(r,z)"
}

Response:

{
  "status": "completed",
  "mri_zones": [...],
  "growth_rates": [...],
  "vorticity_field": "<binary-field-hash>"
}

4.3 Stress Transformation

POST /stability/transform

Applies shear and exotic‑matter transformation matrices.

Body:

{
  "stress_tensor": "sigma_ij",
  "shear_matrix": "S",
  "exotic_matrix": "E"
}

Response:

{
  "stability": "stable | unstable",
  "eigenvalues": [...],
  "pockets": [...]
}

4.4 Cryptographic Provenance

POST /provenance/sign

Signs and chains simulation snapshots.

Body:

{
  "snapshot_hash": "<sha256>",
  "previous_signature": "<sha256>"
}

Response:

{
  "signature": "<sha256>",
  "chain_valid": true
}

4.5 Snapshot Retrieval

GET /snapshot/{id}

Returns encrypted simulation snapshot.

Response:

{
  "snapshot_id": "<uuid>",
  "encrypted_payload": "<base64>"
}

4.6 Topology Visualization Hook

GET /visualization/topology

Returns topology metadata for rendering.

Response:

{
  "helix_path": [...],
  "mri_zones": [...],
  "stability_pockets": [...],
  "vorticity_surfaces": [...]
}

